# Rust build artifacts
/target/

**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# This is a binary crate, not a library, so the lockfile is part of the build
# definition: it pins all 109 transitive packages (axum, rusqlite, tokio and
# their trees). Ignore it and each build silently resolves whatever crates.io
# serves that day -- a dependency can change behaviour, or fail to compile,
# with no commit to point at.
#
# The other two crates in this repo (stitcher/, subtitle_forge/) previously
# ignored their lockfiles. That is why the repository shipped none, and why
# CI had to run `cargo generate-lockfile` before every build.